  "summary": "The code contains a critical path traversal vulnerability, hardcoded configuration, and lacks basic documentation and performance optimizations. I have secured the file path resolution, externalized the configuration, added type hints, and included a docstring to improve overall maintainability and security.",
  "fixed_code": "import os\nfrom flask import Flask, abort, request, send_file, Response\nfrom werkzeug.utils import secure_filename\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\nEXPORT_DIR = os.environ.get('EXPORT_DIR', '/srv/exports')\n\n@app.route(\"/exports/download\")\ndef download_export() -> Response:\n    \"\"\"Downloads a CSV export file by name. Expects 'name' query parameter ending in .csv.\"\"\"\n    raw_name = request.args.get(\"name\")\n    if not raw_name or not raw_name.endswith(\".csv\"):\n        abort(400)\n    \n    # Sanitize filename and validate path\n    safe_name = secure_filename(raw_name)\n    path = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(EXPORT_DIR, safe_name))\n    \n    if not path.startswith(os.path.abspath(EXPORT_DIR)):\n        abort(403)\n        \n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        abort(404)\n        \n    return send_file(path, as_attachment=True)"
